                <pb facs="0126" n="92" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg92"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 59.</note>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Received 9.50 a. m., August 13,
                        1870.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. E. B. Washburne to Mr. Fish.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1870-08-12"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >August 12, 1870.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fish,</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Washington:</hi></p>
                <p>French government decides North Germans, with certain exceptions, quit France.
                    Advise Prussian government and instruct me. Impossible for great numbers of poor
                    to leave without pecuniary aid.</p>
                <p>Will Prussian government place a credit at my disposition to assist poor in
                    leaving? It seems necessary in the interest of humanity.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WASHBURNE, <hi rendition="#italic">Paris.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
